Register custom editors while the workbench starts, not when the browser next
goes idle.

`ICustomEditorService` builds the contributed-editor list and hands it to the
editor resolver in its constructor: it is the only thing that teaches the
workbench that a .png opens as Image Preview, a .ipynb as a notebook, and so on
for every extension-contributed editor. Upstream registers it Delayed, which
means "instantiate when a consumer *uses* it" - a consumer that only holds the
reference gets a proxy backed by a requestIdleCallback. The one startup consumer
(ComplexCustomWorkingCopyEditorHandler, whose ICustomEditorService argument
carries a "DO NOT REMOVE (needed on startup to register overrides properly)"
comment) never touches it, so nothing but that idle callback can build it.

requestIdleCallback here is passed no timeout, and a hidden document never gets
one. Start a window in a background tab - a phone that locks or switches apps
while the workbench loads, an installed app restored into the background - and
no custom editor is registered for the entire life of that window: images open
as "The file is not displayed in the text editor because it is either binary or
uses an unsupported text encoding". Reproduced on Chrome 148 with a hidden tab:
a workspace .png still resolved to the plain text editor 20s after startup, and
"Reopen Editor With..." offered only Text Editor.

It looks intermittent because the list is also cached in browser storage. The
first window that does happen to be visible stores it, and every later window
registers early from that cache - so the capability appears to switch on for
good once something has stored it.

Eager means "instantiate as soon as a consumer depends on it", which is the
startup contribution above, at a fixed point in the boot instead of whenever
the browser feels idle.

--- a/lib/vscode/src/vs/workbench/contrib/customEditor/browser/customEditor.contribution.ts
+++ b/lib/vscode/src/vs/workbench/contrib/customEditor/browser/customEditor.contribution.ts
@@ -16,7 +16,7 @@
 import { CustomEditorDiffInput, CustomEditorSideBySideDiffInput } from './customEditorDiffInput.js';
 import { CustomEditorService } from './customEditors.js';
 
-registerSingleton(ICustomEditorService, CustomEditorService, InstantiationType.Delayed);
+registerSingleton(ICustomEditorService, CustomEditorService, InstantiationType.Eager);
 
 Registry.as<IEditorPaneRegistry>(EditorExtensions.EditorPane)
 	.registerEditorPane(
